## Key Learning

Through this task, the CampusFound functional requirements were converted into structured Java domain models. The main real-world entities of the Lost and Found system were represented using classes, objects, enums, encapsulation, abstraction, and composition. These domain models provide the foundation for implementing the matching, ownership verification, claim management, handover, and item-expiry functionality of CampusFound.
